      {
        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I want to make my breakfasts healthier. Any ideas?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can I have more healthy breakfasts?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To make your breakfasts healthier, consider these ideas:\n\n1. **Eggs**: They are versatile and can be cooked in various ways, such as boiled, scrambled, or as an omelet with vegetables.\n\n2. **Smoothies**: Blend yogurt or plant-based milk with your favorite fruits and some greens like spinach or kale for added nutrients.\n\n3. **Oatmeal**: Use steel-cut oats for more fiber and protein. Top with nuts and berries for extra flavor and nutrition.\n\n4. **Avocado Toast**: Spread mashed avocado on whole-grain bread and add toppings like cherry tomatoes, radishes, or a poached egg.\n\n5. **Sweet Potato Toast**: Slice sweet potatoes and toast them, then top with ingredients like ricotta, berries, or nut butter.\n\n6. **Yogurt Parfait**: Layer plain yogurt with fresh fruits and a sprinkle of granola or nuts for crunch.\n\n7. **Whole-Grain Bread**: Opt for whole-grain or multigrain bread topped with protein-rich spreads like peanut butter or cottage cheese.\n\nThese options are nutrient-dense and can help you feel fuller longer while keeping your breakfasts delicious!",
          "citations": {
