      {
        "turn": 4,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Is brown rice really that much better? Or is quinoa a better choice if I want more protein?",
          "user_rubrik": "How much calcium should I consume daily as a 25 year-old woman?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 0,
          "text": "Brown rice is generally considered healthier than white rice due to its higher fiber and nutrient content, as it retains the bran and germ layers. However, quinoa is even more nutritious, offering more protein and fiber per serving than both white and brown rice. Quinoa is a complete protein, meaning it contains all essential amino acids, which makes it an excellent choice if you're looking to increase your protein intake. Additionally, quinoa has a lower glycemic index than both types of rice, which helps in maintaining stable blood sugar levels. If you're prioritizing protein, quinoa would be the better choice.",
