          "user_utterance": "Do you have tips for making white rice healthier, or should I swap it for something else?",
          "user_rubrik": "How much calcium should I consume daily as a 25 year-old woman?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 0,
          "text": "To make white rice healthier, consider the following tips:\n\n1. **Rinse Before Cooking**: Rinsing the rice thoroughly can help remove excess starch and potential toxins, making it healthier.\n\n2. **Pair with Nutrient-Dense Foods**: Instead of making rice the main part of your meal, serve it alongside a source of protein (like chicken or beans) and plenty of vegetables. This combination helps balance the meal and mitigates the glycemic impact of the rice.\n\n3. **Use Flavorful Cooking Liquids**: Instead of water, cook your rice in vegetable or chicken broth to enhance flavor without adding extra calories or fat.\n\n4. **Add Vegetables and Herbs**: Incorporate steamed or saut\u00e9ed vegetables and fresh herbs into your rice to boost its nutritional profile and flavor.\n\n5. **Limit Portion Size**: Keep your serving of rice small and focus on larger portions of vegetables and lean proteins to maintain a balanced diet.\n\nIf you're looking for alternatives, consider swapping white rice for brown rice, quinoa, or other whole grains, which offer more fiber and nutrients. These options can help you feel fuller and provide better overall health benefits.",
