          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Here are some ideas to make your breakfasts healthier:\n\n1. **Focus on Protein and Fiber**: Aim for at least 5 grams of protein and fiber in your breakfast. Consider options like low-fat yogurt, cottage cheese, or eggs, paired with whole grains like oatmeal or whole-grain bread.\n\n2. **Incorporate Vegetables**: Add non-starchy vegetables to your breakfast. If you\u2019re not a fan of veggies, try blending them into smoothies or adding them to omelets.\n\n3. **Choose Whole Grains**: Opt for whole-grain cereals, breads, or oatmeal instead of refined carbohydrates. Look for cereals with less than 10 grams of sugar and at least 3 grams of fiber per serving.\n\n4. **Healthy Fats**: Include sources of healthy fats, such as avocado, nuts, or seeds. These can help improve blood sugar levels and keep you full longer.\n\n5. **Smoothies**: Blend your favorite fruits and vegetables with yogurt or milk for a quick and nutritious option. You can also add protein powder for an extra boost.\n\n6. **Nut Butter on Toast**: Spread natural peanut butter or almond butter on whole-grain",
