          "user_utterance": "Got it, thanks! Now, what are some low-carb and calcium-rich foods I could use as rice substitutes?",
          "user_rubrik": "How much calories do brown rice, quinoa, cauliflower rice, and black rice have?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 2,
          "text": "Some low-carb and calcium-rich foods you can use as rice substitutes include:\n\n1. **Cauliflower Rice**: Very low in carbs and provides some calcium. It can be easily made by grating cauliflower or purchasing it pre-riced.\n\n2. **Shirataki Rice**: This is a zero-calorie, low-carb option made from konjac root, which is also a good source of fiber but doesn't provide calcium.\n\n3. **Broccoli Rice**: When processed into rice-sized pieces, broccoli provides a good amount of calcium and is low in carbs.\n\n4. **Cabbage Rice**: Chopped cabbage can serve as a rice substitute, is low in carbs, and contains some calcium.\n\n5. **Quinoa**: Although slightly higher in carbs than the others, quinoa is a complete protein and contains calcium, making it a nutritious choice in moderation.\n\nThese alternatives can help you maintain a low-carb diet while boosting your calcium intake.",
