      {
        "turn": 6,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks, that's very clear! Now I want to ask\u2014how healthy are stevia, maple syrup, molasses, and honey compared to sugar?",
          "user_rubrik": "How healthy are stevia, maple syrup, molasses, and honey compared to sugar?\u00a0",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Stevia, maple syrup, molasses, and honey are all healthier alternatives to regular sugar, but they differ in their nutritional profiles and effects on health. \n\n1. **Stevia**: This is considered the healthiest option as it has zero calories and does not raise blood sugar levels, making it safe for diabetics. It is derived from a plant and is much sweeter than sugar, so you need less of it.\n\n2. **Maple Syrup**: While it contains more calories than stevia, maple syrup has some beneficial nutrients and antioxidants. It has a lower glycemic index than regular sugar, meaning it raises blood sugar levels more slowly.\n\n3. **Molasses**: This is a byproduct of sugar production and contains minerals like calcium, iron, and magnesium. It is less sweet than sugar and can be used in baking, but it also has more calories.\n\n4. **Honey**: Raw honey is a natural sweetener with some health benefits, such as antioxidants and enzymes. It has a lower glycemic index than regular sugar, but it is sweeter, so you can use less. However, it still has more calories than sugar.\n\nIn moderation, these alternatives can be healthier choices compared to",
