          "text": "To make your lunch healthier, consider incorporating nutrient-dense, high-protein, and low-carb options while addressing your calcium concerns. Since you usually eat white rice, you could substitute it with cauliflower rice or quinoa for added nutrients and lower carbs. Pair this with lean proteins like grilled chicken, turkey, or tofu, which are rich in protein and can help you feel fuller longer. Adding a side of steamed spinach or broccoli can boost your calcium intake and provide essential vitamins. If you enjoy dairy, low-fat cottage cheese or Greek yogurt can be a great addition to your meal, offering both protein and calcium. For variety, you might also try tempeh or edamame, which are plant-based proteins that are low in carbs and high in nutrients. These adjustments can help you create a balanced and satisfying lunch that aligns with your dietary goals.",
