          "text": "Stevia, maple syrup, molasses, and honey each have different health profiles compared to sugar. Stevia stands out as a zero-calorie, carb-free sweetener, making it a great option for low-carb diets. It doesn\u2019t raise blood sugar levels and is much sweeter than sugar, so only small amounts are needed. Maple syrup, molasses, and honey are more nutrient-dense than sugar, containing vitamins, minerals, and antioxidants, but they still have similar carb and calorie content to sugar. Molasses, particularly blackstrap molasses, is the most nutrient-rich of the three, offering iron, calcium, and other minerals. However, all three should be consumed in moderation due to their high sugar content. If you\u2019re aiming for low-carb options, stevia is the healthiest choice, while the others can be occasional alternatives for added nutrients.",
