          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To make your breakfasts healthier, consider incorporating high-protein, nutrient-dense options that align with your low-carb preferences and calcium needs. For example, eggs are an excellent choice as they are rich in protein, low in carbs, and provide essential nutrients like vitamin D and calcium. Pairing eggs with spinach can further boost calcium intake while keeping the meal low in carbs. You might also try a Greek yogurt parfait with low-carb granola and berries for a protein-packed, calcium-rich option. Cottage cheese with a handful of nuts or seeds is another great choice, offering both protein and healthy fats. Additionally, you can experiment with low-carb breakfast casseroles or omelets loaded with vegetables like broccoli and bell peppers for added nutrients. These ideas can help you start your day with a balanced, satisfying meal.",
