          "text": "The recommended daily calcium intake for women aged 19-50, including 25-year-olds, is 1,000 mg per day according to major health organizations like the National Osteoporosis Foundation and the Institute of Medicine [DOC-1][DOC-2][DOC-3]. This amount supports bone health and helps prevent future osteoporosis. You can meet this requirement through a combination of dairy products, leafy greens, beans, nuts, and calcium-fortified foods. If you are pregnant or breastfeeding, the recommendation remains at 1,000 mg per day for your age group [DOC-2][DOC-3]. Are you interested in non-dairy sources of calcium?",
