          "user_rubrik": "How can I have more healthy breakfasts?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For a healthier, more nutrient-dense, and low-carb breakfast that boosts protein and calcium (and moves you beyond just jam), here\u2019s what works best for your goals:\n\n**Top Breakfast Strategies:**\n- **Prioritize Protein & Calcium:** Include low-fat dairy (Greek yogurt, cottage cheese, or milk), eggs, or tofu. These are high in both protein and calcium (e.g., 1 cup skim milk = 10g protein, 300mg calcium).\n- **Low-Carb Swaps:** Replace refined breads with high-protein, low-carb options like eggs (boiled, scrambled, or as an omelet with veggies), Greek yogurt parfaits (add nuts/seeds, berries), or cottage cheese with sliced cucumber/tomato.\n- **Add Fiber & Nutrients:** Pair your protein with a small portion of berries or leafy greens for extra vitamins and fiber, without spiking carbs.\n- **Upgrade Your Jam Habit:** If you love jam, try swirling a spoonful into plain Greek yogurt or cottage cheese for flavor, but skip the toast to keep carbs low.",
