          "text": "Here\u2019s a clear calorie comparison for the grains you asked about, tailored to your nutrient- and protein-focused, low-carb preferences:\n\n**Calorie Content per 1 Cup (Cooked):**\n- **Cauliflower Rice:** ~25 calories (very low-carb, nutrient-rich, ideal for your goals)\n- **Brown Rice:** ~215\u2013218 calories (higher carb, less protein than quinoa)\n- **Quinoa:** ~220\u2013229 calories (slightly more protein and nutrients than brown rice, but still moderate carbs)\n- **Black Rice:** ~200 calories (similar to brown rice, but with more antioxidants; still higher carb)\n\n**Best for You:**  \nCauliflower rice is by far the lowest in calories and carbs, making it the best fit for your low-carb, nutrient-dense approach. Quinoa is a better grain choice than brown or black rice for protein and minerals, but still higher in carbs than cauliflower.\n\nWould you like ideas for high-protein, low-carb meals using these grains?",
