          "user_utterance": "Great tips! What about healthy lunch options? What should I consider for that?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can I have more healthy lunchs as opposed to breakfast?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For a healthier, more nutrient-dense, high-protein, low-carb lunch that boosts calcium and moves you beyond white rice, here\u2019s what works best for your goals:\n\n**Top Lunch Strategies:**\n\n- **Swap White Rice:** Replace with riced cauliflower or quinoa (quinoa is higher in protein and calcium than rice, and is a complete protein).\n- **Prioritize Protein:** Build your lunch around lean proteins\u2014grilled chicken, tuna, salmon, eggs, tofu, or cottage cheese (which is especially high in both protein and calcium).\n- **Add Calcium-Rich Sides:** Include leafy greens (spinach, kale), broccoli, or a side of Greek yogurt or cottage cheese.\n- **Low-Carb, High-Nutrient Additions:** Add avocado, nuts, seeds, or a small portion of beans/chickpeas for fiber and minerals.\n- **Salad Power Bowls:** Try a large salad with your favorite protein, leafy greens, cherry tomatoes, cucumber, and a sprinkle of seeds or cheese.\n\n**Sample Lunch Ideas:**\n- Grilled chicken or salmon",
