          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks for those suggestions! I'm curious, how much calcium should I consume daily as a 25-year-old woman?",
          "user_rubrik": "How much calcium should I consume daily as a 25 year-old woman?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "As a 25-year-old woman, your recommended daily calcium intake is **1,000 mg** (clueweb22-en0044-22-08373, clueweb22-en0035-97-16082, clueweb22-en0026-68-03614, clueweb22-en0013-71-07330). This applies whether or not you are pregnant or breastfeeding at your age.\n\n**Key points for your goals:**\n- **Why 1,000 mg?** This amount supports bone health and helps prevent future osteoporosis, especially important for women (clueweb22-en0018-21-12818).\n- **How to reach it:** Prioritize calcium-rich, high-protein, low-carb foods like Greek yogurt, cottage cheese, tofu, leafy greens, and canned salmon with bones. Dairy is the most concentrated source, but fortified plant milks and certain vegetables also help (clueweb22-en0026-68-03614).\n- **Vitamin D matters:** Your body needs vitamin D to absorb calcium efficiently. Consider a supplement or ensure",
