          "text": "To make your lunch healthier, consider packing your own lunch with leftovers or ingredients like whole grains, lean proteins, and plenty of fruits and vegetables. Avoid eating out, as it's often more expensive and less healthy. You can also prep your lunches in advance, using methods like freezing meals or making salads with homemade dressings. Additionally, try to include a balance of protein, healthy fats, and complex carbohydrates in your lunch to keep you full and satisfied until dinner time. This can help you save money, reduce food waste, and eat a more balanced diet.",
