          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Yes, consider a Greek yogurt parfait with nuts and berries, or scrambled eggs with spinach and feta cheese. You can also try a smoothie with calcium-fortified almond milk, protein powder, and leafy greens like kale. These options are high in calcium and protein, and can be adapted to be low in carbs. Additionally, you can add some healthy fats like avocado or chia seeds to keep you full until lunch. These ideas should help you start your day with a nutrient-rich breakfast.",
          "citations": {},
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 4,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Those sound tasty! Actually, I often eat white rice for lunch. Do you have suggestions for switching up my lunches to something healthier\u2014maybe with more protein and calcium?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can I have more healthy lunchs as opposed to breakfast?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "You can try replacing white rice with quinoa or brown rice, which are higher in fiber and nutrients. Adding protein sources like grilled chicken, fish, or tofu can also boost the nutritional value of your lunch. Consider incorporating calcium-rich foods like cheese, yogurt, or leafy greens into your meals. A salad with grilled chicken, avocado, and a citrus vinaigrette could be a healthy and satisfying option. You can also try making a soup with vegetables and beans, which are high in protein and fiber. These changes can help you create a more balanced and nutritious lunch.",
          "citations": {},
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Cool ideas! What about cake? I bake every week\u2014are there ways to make my cakes a bit healthier, maybe with extra calcium or protein?",
