          "user_rubrik_score": 0,
          "text": "You can make healthier cakes by using whole wheat flour, adding nuts or seeds, and incorporating calcium-rich ingredients like Greek yogurt or milk. Consider using protein powder or nut butters to boost the protein content. You can also reduce the sugar content by using natural sweeteners like honey or maple syrup. Additionally, try adding some calcium-fortified milk or cheese to your cake recipes. These modifications can help make your cakes a bit healthier while still satisfying your sweet tooth. Experiment with different ingredients to find a balance that works for you.",
          "citations": {},
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 6,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks, that helps! But I still wonder: How much calcium should I consume daily as a 25 year-old woman?",
          "user_rubrik": "How much calcium should I consume daily as a 25 year-old woman?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "As a 25-year-old woman, the recommended daily calcium intake is around 1,000 milligrams. This can be achieved through a combination of calcium-rich foods, such as dairy products, leafy greens, and fortified plant-based milk, as well as supplements if necessary. It's also important to note that your body absorbs calcium more efficiently when it's consumed in smaller amounts throughout the day, rather than in one large dose. You can consult with a healthcare professional or a registered dietitian to determine the best calcium intake plan for your individual needs. They can help you create a personalized plan to ensure you're getting enough calcium to support your overall health.",
          "citations": {},
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 7,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Got it, thanks! By the way, how many calories do brown rice, quinoa, cauliflower rice, and black rice usually have?",
