          "ptkb_provenance": [
            "1. I am interested in low-carb food.",
            "2. I prefer foods with more nutrients and protein.",
            "3. I think I don't get enough calcium, and I am worried about it.",
            "4. I eat jam for breakfast.",
            "5. I like the taste of white bread."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 2,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Interesting! I do tend to have more variety for breakfast than for lunch, though. How can I make my lunches just as healthy, especially if I usually eat white rice?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can I have more healthy lunchs as opposed to breakfast?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To make your lunches healthier, especially if you usually eat white rice, consider low-carb alternatives like riced cauliflower, shirataki rice, or riced broccoli. These are great for reducing carbs. For a protein boost, pair your chosen rice alternative with lean proteins such as grilled chicken, salmon, tofu, or beans. Quinoa and wild rice are also excellent, higher-protein grain alternatives. To boost calcium, include leafy greens like kale in your meal, or consider adding low-fat cheese or yogurt if it fits your lunch.",
          "citations": {
