        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Hi! I\u2019m looking for ways to make my breakfasts healthier. What are some good ideas?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can I have more healthy breakfasts?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To make your breakfasts healthier, focusing on low-carb, high-protein options that boost calcium is key. Instead of white bread and jam, consider low-carb breads made from almond or coconut flour, or top your toast with protein like eggs.\n\nGreek yogurt is an excellent choice: it's low-carb, rich in protein, and a good source of calcium. Enjoy it with berries and almonds, or blend into a smoothie with spinach or kale for extra nutrients. Eggs are another versatile, high-protein, low-carb option; try them scrambled with spinach or as part of a breakfast muffin. Other calcium-rich foods include collard greens, kale, and chia seeds.",
