          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s interesting\u2014thanks! Changing topics a little bit: how healthy are stevia, maple syrup, molasses, and honey compared to sugar?",
          "user_rubrik": "How healthy are stevia, maple syrup, molasses, and honey compared to sugar?\u00a0",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Stevia is generally considered the healthiest option as it's calorie-free, carb-free, and doesn't affect blood sugar levels. Maple syrup, molasses, and honey are \"less bad\" than refined sugar, offering some trace minerals, vitamins, and antioxidants. For instance, maple syrup contains calcium, potassium, and zinc, while honey has iron and copper, and both may have a lower glycemic index than sugar. However, they still contain significant sugar and calories, so moderation is key.",
