          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I want to make my breakfasts healthier. Any ideas?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can I have more healthy breakfasts?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For healthier breakfasts, focus on high-protein, low-carb, and calcium-rich foods. Greek yogurt is excellent: high in protein, rich in calcium, and low-carb. Enjoy it with berries and almonds, or blend into a smoothie with protein powder and spinach. Eggs are another versatile, high-protein, low-carb option; try them scrambled with spinach. For more calcium, low-fat cheese is a good choice. Instead of white bread and jam, opt for whole grain bread, or consider low-carb alternatives like chia seed jam with yogurt or baked goods made with almond/coconut flour.",
