      {
        "turn": 2,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks, that helps! But actually, I have trouble making healthy lunches, not just breakfasts. What changes can I make for lunch?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can I have more healthy lunchs as opposed to breakfast?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For healthier lunches, consider replacing white rice with options like brown rice, wild rice, or cauliflower rice, which offer more nutrients, fiber, and are lower in carbs. To boost protein and calcium, add lean proteins such as chicken, fish, tofu, or eggs. Include low-fat cheese or yogurt in your meals. Incorporate plenty of vegetables and healthy fats like avocado or nuts to increase fiber and nutrients. For example, try a salad with brown rice, chicken, and cheese, or a chicken and spinach dish with cheese.",
