          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s super helpful. Does cauliflower rice have less protein than the others?",
          "user_rubrik": "How healthy are stevia, maple syrup, molasses, and honey compared to sugar?\u00a0",
          "user_rubrik_score": 0,
          "text": "Yes, cauliflower rice generally has less protein than brown rice, quinoa, and black rice. Per 100 grams, cauliflower rice has about 1.9g of protein, brown rice has about 2.7g, and quinoa has about 4.4g. While a specific amount for black rice isn't provided, it contains more protein than white rice (which has about 2.4g per 100g), indicating it also surpasses cauliflower rice.",
