          "user_utterance": "Thanks, that sounds great! But honestly, my lunches tend to be less healthy than breakfast. How can I improve that?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can I have more healthy lunchs as opposed to breakfast?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To make your lunches healthier, shift from white rice to high-protein, low-carb options. Consider brown rice with lean protein like chicken, tofu, or paneer, and lots of vegetables (P1, P12). Salads are excellent, packed with protein from grilled chicken, salmon, or eggs, and abundant leafy greens (P6, P10, P19). Other great choices include lettuce wraps (P2), cauliflower rice with protein (P3), or a hearty lentil/bean soup (P8). These nutrient-rich meals will keep you full and energized, preventing afternoon slumps (P4, P15).",
