      {
        "turn": 2,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks, that sounds good! I usually focus on breakfast, but what about lunch? How can I make my lunches even healthier compared to breakfast?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can I have more healthy lunchs as opposed to breakfast?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For healthier, low-carb, and high-protein lunches, consider replacing white rice with cauliflower fried rice. Salads are excellent options, such as tuna and egg salad, or those with grilled chicken, salmon, or halloumi cheese, which also provides calcium. Lettuce wraps with lean protein like turkey or chicken are another great choice. You could also try paneer or tofu dishes for protein, or avocado chicken bowls.",
