          "user_utterance": "Oh, I had no idea it was 1,000 mg! Does cauliflower rice or any of those substitutes have much calcium compared to white rice?",
          "user_rubrik": "How much calories do brown rice, quinoa, cauliflower rice, and black rice have?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 0,
          "text": "One cup of cauliflower rice contains 19 mg of calcium, significantly more than white rice, which has only 1 mg. This is a small step towards your 1,000 mg daily goal. For other lunch alternatives, 100 grams of tofu can provide up to 176 mg of calcium, and a cup of butterhead lettuce has 19 mg. Adding canned salmon or sardines to salads can also significantly boost your calcium intake, providing up to 30% of your daily recommended amount.",
