        "turn": 6,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "No worries, that answered most of it! I\u2019m interested in swapping out sugar in my baked goods sometimes. How healthy are stevia, maple syrup, molasses, and honey compared to sugar?",
          "user_rubrik": "How healthy are stevia, maple syrup, molasses, and honey compared to sugar?\u00a0",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Stevia is generally considered the healthiest sugar substitute for baking, as it's plant-derived, has no calories, and is much sweeter than sugar, so you use less. Natural sweeteners like maple syrup, molasses, and honey are less harmful than regular sugar and offer health benefits like nutrients and antioxidants. Maple syrup has a lower glycemic index than sugar and honey. Honey also has a lower GI than sugar but more calories. While these are better options, they still contain calories and sugar, so moderation is key.",
