  {
    "runtag": "uva-gpt5-bm25-debertav3-gpt5",
    "type": "ikat-dialog-v1",
    "topic": "5-1",
    "responses": [
      {
        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I want to know how to make my breakfasts healthier. Any ideas?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can I have more healthy breakfasts?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "great question! here are easy, nutrient - dense, higher \u2011 protein breakfast ideas that support low - carb eating and your calcium goals : - greek or skyr yogurt parfait : layer zero \u2011 sugar yogurt with berries, a sprinkle of low \u2011 carb granola, chia / flax, and a few nuts. big protein and calcium. - egg muffins ( meal \u2011 prep ) : eggs or egg whites with spinach, ham, and cheese baked in a muffin tin. reheat and go. - cottage cheese bowl : top with cinnamon, berries, and walnuts or peanut butter. high protein, good calcium. - chia pudding : mix chia with unsweetened almond / soy milk, vanilla, and a little sweetener ; chill overnight. add berries and almonds. - flax \u201c oatmeal \u201d : stir hot water into ground flax, add cinnamon, butter or nut butter, and a splash of milk. - 1 \u2011 minute protein pancake in a mug : almond flour, egg, cinnamon, sweetener ; microwave. top with greek yogurt and sugar \u2011 free jam. - toast upgrade : if you love white bread,",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0002-41-08921:1": -1.9589462280273438,
            "clueweb22-en0028-93-01206:2": -2.8388376235961914,
            "clueweb22-en0043-24-07369:0": -2.847351551055908,
            "clueweb22-en0010-18-13621:8": -2.9216341972351074,
            "clueweb22-en0005-52-13253:4": -3.095688819885254
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 2,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks! Those breakfast ideas sound yummy. But what about lunch? How could I make my lunches as healthy as these breakfasts? Like, more nutrients and maybe more protein?",
          "user_rubrik": "How can I have more healthy lunchs as opposed to breakfast?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "great question! here are easy, meal \u2011 prep lunches that are higher in protein, nutrient \u2011 dense, and friendly to low \u2011 carb goals ( with calcium boosts ) : - chicken fajita lunch bowls ( eaten cold ) : grilled chicken, bell peppers, red onion, lime \u2011 chili vinaigrette over cauliflower rice or half cauli / half basmati. add a little shredded cheese for calcium. - salmon \u201c sushi \u201d bowl : cauliflower rice, baked salmon, cucumber, avocado, nori, sesame ; drizzle sriracha \u2011 greek \u2011 yogurt for extra protein and calcium. - burger bowl : romaine / spinach, lean ground beef or turkey, tomatoes, pickles, onions, a sprinkle of cheddar ; dressing = greek yogurt + mustard + relish. - southwest bbq chicken salad : bbq chicken, black beans, corn, butter lettuce, cilantro \u2011 lime dressing ; add cotija or feta for calcium. - spicy shrimp + crispy rice + kale : pan \u2011 sear leftover rice for crunch ( or use cauliflower rice ), toss with kale",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0020-51-15640:2": -0.7857670783996582,
            "clueweb22-en0002-28-18619:12": -1.0868641138076782,
