      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "These lunch ideas sound delicious, especially the salmon bowl! Quick question: Is there a specific amount of calcium I should be aiming for daily as a woman my age?",
          "user_rubrik": "How much calcium should I consume daily as a 25 year-old woman?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For a 25-year-old woman, aim for 1,000 mg of calcium per day. Don\u2019t exceed 2,500 mg/day. Your body absorbs only about 300\u2013500 mg at a time, so spread calcium across meals.  Food first: - About three servings of dairy typically meets 1,000 mg (milk, Greek/skyr yogurt, cheese). - Non-dairy options: dark leafy greens and calcium\u2011fortified milks/foods.  Label tip: % Daily Value for calcium \u00d7 10 \u2248 milligrams (e.g., 15% \u2248 150 mg).  If you need a supplement, choose calcium citrate. Take it in divided doses no more than 500 mg at once; it can be taken with or without food.  Example day to hit 1,000 mg: - Breakfast: Greek yogurt parfait (~200\u2013300 mg) - Lunch: Salmon bowl with a Greek\u2011yogurt drizzle and a sprinkle of cheese (~200\u2013300 mg) - Snack: Cottage cheese (~100\u2013200 mg) - Dinner: Saut\u00e9ed kale and a cup of milk or fortified milk (~300 mg)",
          "citations": {
