          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "I don\u2019t have your age \u2014 can you tell me? Meanwhile, general targets:  - Ages 9\u201318 (teens): 1,300 mg/day   - Adults 19\u201350: 1,000 mg/day   - Women 51 and older: 1,200 mg/day  These totals include calcium from food plus any supplements. Don\u2019t routinely exceed about 2,000 mg/day (total) because of side-effect risks. Aim to get most calcium from diet (milk/yogurt, fortified plant milks, leafy greens, canned salmon/sardines, tofu), and use supplements only if you can\u2019t meet needs \u2014 talk with your clinician about type/dose and whether you also need vitamin D. Tell me your age and I\u2019ll confirm the right target and a simple plan to reach it.",
